# Optional S3 cache for the OG/social share thumbnails (/share.webp/…).
# When S3_BUCKET + S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID + S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are all set, rendered
# thumbnails are stored in the bucket keyed by route+etag and re-served without
# re-rendering; unset (or any S3 error) falls back to rendering every time.
# S3 requests fail fast (~3s) into the render path. See apps/web/WORKAROUNDS.md.

# S3_PUBLIC_URL / S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT: public base URL of the bucket, when it is
# public-read (#218). When set, cache hits 302-redirect to the public object URL
# instead of proxying the bytes through the web app. Leave unset while the bucket
# is private — the redirect target would 403, so unset = proxy-bytes behavior.

# Local dev: the root docker-compose.yml runs a MinIO (S3-compatible) service
# (`podman compose up -d`) with a pre-created, anonymous-download `bgs-assets`
# bucket; console at http://127.0.0.1:9001 (minio / minio123). Uncomment:
# S3_BUCKET=bgs-assets
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minio
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minio123

# Production (Scaleway):
# S3_BUCKET=bgs-assets
# S3_REGION=fr-par
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://s3.fr-par.scw.cloud
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
